{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"knJhq4yFUws7"},"source":["# Learnings\n","- Softmax is `e^x/sum(e^x)`\n","- Log Softmax is `log(e^x/sum(e^x))` = `log(e^x) - log(sum(e^x))` = `x - log(sum(e^x))`\n","- Log Softmax is used because\n","  - NLLoss/CELoss work with log probs\n","  - It is numerically more stable\n","- CE Loss = LogSoftmax + NLL\n","  - LogSoftmax is above\n","  - NLL = You just collect all the losses at the GT index and calculate their mean and then -ve it. so NLL = -1 * sum(log_softmax @ the GT index)\n","- In Pytorch, `tensor[[0,1], [0,1]]` will get `tensor[0][0]` and `tensor[1][1]`\n","  - `preds[2:5, :2]` this shit is same as in numpy"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"HXFd-8cQUoKm"},"outputs":[],"source":["# https://docs.pytorch.org/tutorials/beginner/nn_tutorial.html"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"pF-K_RZrUyT3"},"outputs":[],"source":["import torch"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"metadata":{"id":"2376706rUzGC","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1771826642418,"user_tz":480,"elapsed":597,"user":{"displayName":"Nikhit Mago","userId":"05688642061475705858"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["from pathlib import Path\n","import requests\n","\n","DATA_PATH = Path(\"data\")\n","PATH = DATA_PATH / \"mnist\"\n","\n","PATH.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n","\n","URL = \"https://github.com/pytorch/tutorials/raw/main/_static/\"\n","FILENAME = \"mnist.pkl.gz\"\n","\n","if not (PATH / FILENAME).exists():\n","        content = requests.get(URL + FILENAME).content\n","        (PATH / FILENAME).open(\"wb\").write(content)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"metadata":{"id":"-71ZTJ-bWHBn","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1771826645236,"user_tz":480,"elapsed":1173,"user":{"displayName":"Nikhit Mago","userId":"05688642061475705858"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["import pickle\n","import gzip\n","\n","with gzip.open((PATH / FILENAME).as_posix(), \"rb\") as f:\n